ays that running \"kiru\" then \"kifu\" is same as \"kifu\" alone. So if \"kiru\" is applied to BARU, and then \"kifu\" is applied, the result is same as \"kifu\" alone. That implies that applying \"kiru\" doesn't change the result of \"kifu\". Therefore, \"kiru\" must act as the identity on the BARU slots.", "class": "INVALID", "logprobs": {"sum_logprob": -2951.9638281923008, "n_tokens": 12000}, "answer_chars": 38894}
